# Beads JSONL files are one-way, DERIVED exports of the Dolt board. The real
# source of truth is the Dolt history synced via refs/dolt/data on origin, which
# merges at the cell level and never text-conflicts. These exports, by contrast,
# are plain text that sessions re-generate — so parallel / ephemeral cloud
# containers collide on the same lines and produce spurious merge conflicts.
#
# `merge=union` is a BUILT-IN git merge strategy (no .git/config driver to
# register, so it works on every fresh clone including cold cloud containers). It
# tells git to keep BOTH sides instead of raising conflict markers. Any transient
# duplicate / stale row is harmless: the next `bd export` rewrites the file clean
# from the authoritative board. NEVER hand-resolve these files.
*.jsonl merge=union
